    "body": "- **feat(pick): pass actions to custom mapping function**\n- **docs(pick): document custom mapping function**\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\nHey, I suggest to pass table with actions to custom mapping function. This\nallow more customization. E.g. I want to configure keybindings similar to fzf.\nIn fzf `<Tab>` mark current item and move to next. To reproduce this in\nMini.Pick I need access to actions in my custom mapping function.\n\nHow I used this you can see in my [config](https://github.com/feelamee/dotfiles/blob/5ce29b6d769ab51d33b12f0304fd5433e76a5a74/nvim/init.lua#L188).\n\nThis feature don't introduce breaking changes. That's why it can be easily merged.\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-04-06T12:09:53Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nAlthough implementing \"mark and move down\" functionality does indeed look straightforward, I think this (constructing the all action functions) is a bit too much to do on every picker advance.\r\n\r\nThe recommended approach of using built-in actions is to get picker's `mapping` data and use `vim.api.nvim_input()` to simulate pressing those keys. This was discussed in #1339. Here is a more general solution for Neovim>=0.10:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal input_actions = function(actions)\r\n  return function()\r\n    local mappings = MiniPick.get_picker_opts().mappings\r\n    local keys = vim.tbl_map(function(a) return mappings[a] end, actions)\r\n    vim.api.nvim_input(vim.keycode(table.concat(keys)))\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    -- Don't use built-in <Tab> and <S-Tab>\r\n    toggle_preview = '<C-l>',\r\n    toggle_info = '<C-h>',\r\n    scroll_left = '',\r\n    scroll_right = '',\r\n\r\n    -- Use <Tab> and <S-Tab> to mark+move\r\n    mark_and_down = { char = '<Tab>', func = input_actions({ 'mark', 'move_down' }) },\r\n    mark_and_up = { char = '<S-Tab>', func = input_actions({ 'mark', 'move_up' }) },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I am going to close this as \"a bit too much because it is already possible\".",
